course: dictionary
lesson: 8645
title: One word, many meanings: seal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The meaning depends on the words around it, which are its context. «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost.» A pup is a baby animal, so here seal means a sea animal.
explain: «The jar was sealed with a lid to keep the food fresh.» Here seal is a verb, an action word. It means to close something tightly so nothing gets in or out. Check by swapping in the meaning: "The jar was closed tightly with a lid to keep the food fresh" still makes sense.
explain: «The old letter had a red wax seal to show it was real.» Here seal means a special stamp or mark that proves a document is genuine. The clue words are letter and real.
explain: When you meet a word you know, do not stop there. Ask: which meaning fits the clues in this sentence?
fact: A seal is a sea animal with a smooth body, flippers and thick fat. It lives in the sea and on land.
fact: Seals are mammals, not fish: they breathe air, have fur and feed their pups milk.
fact: «To seal» means to close something tightly, so nothing gets in or out.
fact: A seal can also be a special stamp or mark, often in wax, put on a document to show it is real.
fact: «Seal of approval» means someone has said that something is good.
exercise: «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost.» In this sentence, what is a seal? | *A sea animal | A lid on a jar | A stamp on a letter | A type of fish
exercise: «The jar was sealed to keep the food fresh.» What does sealed mean here? | Thrown away | Painted bright red | *Closed tightly | Opened wide
exercise: «The old document had a wax seal to show it was real.» What is the seal here? | A sea animal | A hot pan for cooking | A kind of fish | *A special mark that proves a paper is genuine
test: Seals are mammals, not fish. Which is true about them? | *They breathe air and feed their pups milk | They have no flippers | They lay their eggs in water and have no fur | They have scales and gills
test: «A broken seal on a bottle of medicine is a warning sign.» Why? | The bottle is new | *It may mean someone opened it, so it may not be safe | The medicine is sweet | The bottle is full
exam: «Please seal the envelope before you post it.» What does seal mean here? | A special stamp | A kind of fish | *To close something tightly | A sea animal
